---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BrandLogo from '../components/BrandLogo.astro';
import {version, releaseURL, assetURL} from '../data/release';
const home = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout title="Download Dictate — free local dictation">
  <main class="download-page">
    <header><a class="wordmark" href={home}><BrandLogo size={30}/><span>Dictate</span></a><a class="back" href={home}>Back to home</a></header>
    <section class="intro"><h1>Your voice.<br/><em>Your computer.</em></h1><p class="lede">Install Dictate, set up a local model, and start speaking. No account, subscription, or developer tools.</p><p class="release-status">{version} · Community beta</p></section>
    <nav class="platform-links" aria-label="Choose your operating system"><a href="#mac">Mac</a><a href="#windows">Windows</a><a href="#linux">Linux</a></nav>
    <section class="platform" id="mac" aria-labelledby="mac-title">
      <div class="platform-heading"><div><h2 id="mac-title">Mac</h2><p>Apple silicon · macOS 14 or newer</p></div><a class="download" href={assetURL('Dictate.dmg')}>Download for Mac <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
      <ol><li>Open the download and drag Dictate to <strong>Applications</strong>.</li><li>Open Dictate from Applications or Spotlight.</li><li>Allow the microphone, then choose <strong>Set up recommended model</strong>. Allow Accessibility if you want words inserted into other apps.</li></ol>
      <details><summary>If macOS cannot verify the developer</summary><p>This free community build is ad-hoc signed and is not notarized by Apple. After attempting to open the trusted download, go to <strong>System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → Open Anyway</strong>, then confirm. Work computers may require your administrator.</p><p>If the warning explicitly says malware or the app is damaged, stop and check the download and release checksums. This is different from an unverified-developer warning. <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/102445">Read Apple's warning guide ↗</a></p></details>
      <details><summary>Older macOS, Intel, and source builds</summary><p>On macOS 14 and 15, setup uses a downloadable local model. Apple recognition is offered only on compatible macOS 26 devices. The native interface is the same. This beta targets macOS 14; runtime testing on older Macs is still pending. Intel Mac installers are not available.</p><p>You do not need Xcode to use the downloaded app. Compiling the Swift source still requires full Xcode with the macOS 26 SDK.</p><p>Already cloned or extracted the repository? Run <code>./Scripts/start.sh</code> from its folder. It verifies and installs this prebuilt release, preserving your models and history. It does not compile local changes or bypass macOS security.</p></details>
    </section>
    <section class="platform" id="windows" aria-labelledby="windows-title">
      <div class="platform-heading"><div><h2 id="windows-title">Windows <small>Beta</small></h2><p>Windows 10 / 11 · x64</p></div><a class="download" href={assetURL('Dictate-Windows-x64-setup.exe')}>Download for Windows <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
      <ol><li>Open the installer and follow the prompts. It installs for your user account.</li><li>Open Dictate and choose <strong>Set up recommended model</strong> (Whisper Tiny, about 78 MB).</li><li>Start a short recording and allow microphone access if prompted. Use your shortcut in an editable field, or copy the completed text.</li></ol>
      <details><summary>First-launch warnings and compatibility</summary><p>This installer has no paid signing certificate. Windows may show an unknown-publisher or SmartScreen warning. Only proceed with a download you trust; follow your organization's policy. If Microsoft Defender reports malware, do not bypass it.</p><p>The installer can download Microsoft's free WebView2 runtime if it is missing. Model setup also needs internet. Recognition runs locally afterward. Automatic insertion requires an accessible editor at the same or lower privilege level; otherwise, your transcript stays ready to copy.</p><p>This is an initial portable beta. Physical-device microphone and editor testing is still needed; see the release's validation record.</p></details>
    </section>
    <section class="platform" id="linux" aria-labelledby="linux-title">
      <div class="platform-heading"><div><h2 id="linux-title">Linux <small>Beta</small></h2><p>x64 · Ubuntu 22.04+ / compatible distributions</p></div><a class="download" href={assetURL('Dictate-Linux-x64.deb')}>Download .deb <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
      <ol><li>Open the <strong>.deb</strong> in your software installer. For other distributions, try the <a href={assetURL('Dictate-Linux-x64.AppImage')}>AppImage</a> and allow execution in its file properties.</li><li>Open Dictate and set up the recommended local model (about 78 MB).</li><li>Press <strong>Record</strong>, speak, then finish. Copy your words into your destination.</li></ol>
      <details><summary>X11, Wayland, and system dependencies</summary><p>X11 supports a global shortcut and attempts insertion into an accessible focused editor through AT-SPI. On Wayland, this beta uses the Record button and copy flow; global shortcuts and automatic insertion are not enabled.</p><p>The .deb installs required system libraries through your package manager. If your AppImage cannot mount because FUSE is unavailable, run <code>./Dictate-Linux-x64.AppImage --appimage-extract-and-run</code>. Compatibility depends on your distribution. Linux microphone, tray, and editor behavior still need device testing.</p></details>
    </section>
    <section class="help"><h2>Local after setup. Free throughout.</h2><p>The app downloads speech models from public repositories. Your recordings are processed on your computer. No API keys, cloud transcription, or paid services are required.</p><p><a href={releaseURL}>Release notes and all downloads ↗</a><a href={assetURL('manifest.json')}>Checksums and file sizes ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/leviackerman05/dictate/blob/main/docs/evidence/portability-validation.md">What has been tested ↗</a></p></section>
    <footer><span>Dictate · Open source under MIT</span><a href="https://github.com/leviackerman05/dictate">View the source ↗</a></footer>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
.download-page{max-width:1080px;margin:auto;padding:0 40px}header,footer{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;padding:30px 0}.wordmark{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;font-size:21px;font-weight:650}.back,footer{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}.intro{padding:56px 0 32px;max-width:680px}.release-status{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:24px}h1{font-size:clamp(48px,7vw,80px);font-weight:500;line-height:1.02;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:24px 0}em{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-weight:400}.lede{font-size:20px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted);max-width:570px}.platform-links{display:flex;gap:12px;margin:0 0 48px}.platform-links a{padding:12px 20px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px}.platform{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:32px 0;scroll-margin-top:20px}.platform-heading{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:18px}.number{color:var(--action);font-size:14px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.platform-heading h2{font-size:29px;font-weight:550;letter-spacing:-.03em;margin:0}.platform-heading p{color:var(--muted);font-size:14px;margin:8px 0}.platform-heading small{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0;background:var(--raised);padding:4px 8px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:5px;vertical-align:middle}.download{margin-left:auto;padding:14px 20px;background:#3155d9;color:#fff;border-radius:9px;display:flex;gap:22px;white-space:nowrap;font-size:14px;font-weight:550}.download:hover{background:#2544ba}ol{padding-left:24px;max-width:770px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--muted);margin:26px 0}li{padding:4px 0}strong{color:var(--text);font-weight:550}details{margin:10px 0;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:0 18px}summary{cursor:pointer;padding:16px 0;font-size:15px}details p{max-width:800px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;font-size:15px}details a,li a,.help a{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;color:var(--action)}code{font-size:13px;background:var(--raised);padding:3px 5px;border-radius:4px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.help{padding:30px 0;border-block:1px solid var(--border);margin-top:20px}.help h2{font-size:26px;font-weight:500}.help p{line-height:1.7;color:var(--muted);max-width:800px}.help a{display:inline-block;margin-right:24px;font-size:14px}footer{padding-bottom:40px}@media(max-width:650px){.download-page{padding:0 22px}.intro{padding-top:30px}.platform-heading{flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px}.download{margin-left:0;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;margin-top:10px}.lede{font-size:18px}.platform-links{margin-bottom:30px}.platform-links a{flex:1;text-align:center;padding-inline:12px}footer{align-items:flex-start;flex-direction:column}ol{font-size:15px}.help a{display:block;margin:12px 0}}
</style>
